{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"f366f51201b7f7ffa4de19257bf0f61b9c1457074f100077694f9081ff83bb1e","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_48e4c9791d510cd9a1a026cd6c514abdba7e0c9c1ff8e028a91da6584312a5ad","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent framework for adaptive computation that is technically sound and well-supported by experiments on a custom physics task. The methodological formulation of the metacontroller as a reinforcement learning problem is clear, and the experimental results convincingly demonstrate the ability to trade off performance and computational cost. However, the evaluation is limited to a single, synthetic task, and the paper lacks comparisons to standard adaptive computation baselines and sufficient implementation details for full reproducibility.","paper_id":"Bk8BvDqex","paper_identity_sha256":"afe65733b755b01ebaee801d2ba3b850d6b9acf3a82a0db4713745ef5215cf6a","prompt_identity_sha256":"26ad1199ccfd3a072d275342f55925fe70e120b57b9180eb3c9f7f3580bfc779","raw_response_sha256":"846dd577d2d2a6167b1555c3b2637b74750bfb330889e1f1c1f10099a5c2c606","request_identity_sha256":"5bf3d92f9238862b1ba065c7144132648aaccb90397f2562e578d199174c91f4","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"d81fa80b34a199b3e084b404ee0cba9547fbf74b87323b2ad6e6337c0df9b7a2","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The proposed metacontroller architecture is well-formulated. The paper clearly defines the optimization objective as a combination of performance loss and computational resource loss, and correctly recasts this as a reinforcement learning problem where the manager policy selects the number of iterations and the specific expert to use. The use of a stochastic policy for the manager, trained with REINFORCE, is an appropriate choice given the discrete nature of the actions (stopping or selecting an expert). The mathematical consistency of the model is maintained throughout, and the distinction between the controller, experts, and manager is logically sound.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The experimental design is adequate for validating the core claims of the paper. The authors use a custom physics-based task (spaceship navigation) with varying levels of difficulty (1 to 5 planets) to test the adaptive nature of the metacontroller. The choice of baselines (reactive and iterative agents) is appropriate for isolating the benefits of the metacontroller's adaptive decision-making. The evaluation metrics, which include both performance loss and total cost (performance plus computation), are well-suited to the paper's objective of optimizing the speed-accuracy trade-off. However, the reliance on a single, synthetic task limits the generalizability of the empirical claims.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018"],"review_text":"The paper provides a high-level description of the neural network implementation, specifying the use of MLPs, LSTMs, and Interaction Networks. However, it lacks the specific hyperparameters, training details, and code availability necessary for full reproducibility. For instance, the exact architecture sizes, learning rates, and training durations for the controller, experts, and manager are not provided in the main text. While the paper references appendices for further details, the absence of these specifics in the main body and the lack of a code release hinder the ability to independently replicate the results.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-006","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper positions its work well within the context of prior research on metareasoning, conditional computation, and adaptive computation time. It appropriately cites foundational work by Russell and Wefald, as well as more recent developments by Graves and Bengio. However, the experimental comparisons are limited to the paper's own baseline agents (reactive and iterative). There is no direct comparison to other state-of-the-art adaptive computation methods, such as Adaptive Computation Time (ACT) or other metareasoning frameworks, which would have provided a stronger benchmark for the proposed approach.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-028"],"review_text":"The paper demonstrates some statistical rigor by reporting confidence intervals for the metacontroller's performance and using regression analysis to show the relationship between task difficulty and the number of ponder steps. The use of 95% confidence intervals in Figure 4 is a positive step. However, the paper does not report the number of independent runs or seeds used to generate the results, which makes it difficult to assess the variance and statistical significance of the reported improvements. The lack of multiple seeds is a notable gap in the statistical validation of the experimental results.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"a7e867b327054c06c32b0fba71f9d7e9744692c900b2782c62b9470c52b73e85","paper_id":"Bk8BvDqex","paper_ordinal":45,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"846dd577d2d2a6167b1555c3b2637b74750bfb330889e1f1c1f10099a5c2c606","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"Bk8BvDqex","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"d35591db03f716945dda25b876ef48d74a6e03c7b4b82aabfb5f3eb15d3f066c","request_identity_sha256":"5bf3d92f9238862b1ba065c7144132648aaccb90397f2562e578d199174c91f4","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1041,"prompt_tokens":17198,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18239},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"5bf3d92f9238862b1ba065c7144132648aaccb90397f2562e578d199174c91f4","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}